  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Maximum <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> (least basic) is (d) since, lone pair on<br />N-atom is used to delocalise <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math> -electrons on two benzene<br />rings.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0003_96906f61408a.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 107px;\" /></p><p>Least basic has maximum value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math>.</p><p>Since, in (d), lone pair of electrons over <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>-atom are delocalised to two benzene rings, thus is least basic.</p>"
